.gradle/
build/
local.properties
.superpowers/
# Harness state, like .superpowers/ above -- written by the tooling, never by the project.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
*.iml
.idea/
*.hprof

# The Kotlin Gradle plugin writes `.kotlin/sessions/<id>.salive` during every build and removes it
# only on a clean shutdown, so any interrupted build leaves it behind. Untracked debris here is not
# harmless: `ci/mutation-probes.sh` refuses to run on a dirty tree (it reverts with
# `git checkout --`, which cannot tell a probe from real work), so without this line an interrupted
# build makes the probe list unrunnable until someone deletes a directory they did not create.
.kotlin/
